  "coverage": [
    "Native quads: all 5 blends, 12 fixture entries, cold/hot headers, mutable XY/UV/color/image dimensions, signed zero, live resolution scales, cover flags, texture dimensions, recycled entry/VRAM address and header invalidation.",
    "Queue ownership: submitted quad inputs are unchanged, then overwritten before draining; queued values survive. Repeated source-address reuse and frame 0 / UINT_MAX are exercised. Null handles and prefix order barriers retain output order.",
    "Admission guards: frame not ready, stream aborted, alpha 0, masked quad, unsupported blend, full queue, missing texture, black/movie state and nonfinite XY/UV.",
    "Bridge: 1,280 cases each with 2 successive source calls; no CLUT/present CLUT, descriptor/texture failures, orthographic/perspective/zero-depth projection, matrix shear/translation, viewport offset/size/jitter, live color/UV/vertex mutation, prompt/mask/letterbox/option callbacks.",
    "Bridge serialization contains every field of the 104-byte target Re4dcUiQuad. Actual host structs have wider pointers; opaque synthetic pointers fit in 32 bits and serialization excludes only host ABI padding.",
    "Glyph emission: counts 0/1/2/15/16/17/31/32/33/64/129/384, palette bank changes, flush boundaries, mixed quad/glyph order, prefix/subrange/empty/end-clamped runs, quarter-pixel limits, degenerate rectangles, color 0, signed-zero/negative/fractional/tiny dynamic scales, stateful overlay depth and unsigned layer wrap.",
    "Camera: 256 restores per profile of full 4x4 matrix and compact GX projection, unchanged viewport, native-disabled fallback.",
    "UI_QUAD_LEAN=2 production mismatch counters assert zero; periodic diagnostics are captured in serialized state.",
    "Public profile ASan+UBSan completes without diagnostics in either arm."
  ],
  "production_bodies_and_types": [
    "native_ui.h Re4dcUiImage/Re4dcUiQuad/Re4dcUiGlyph; IdUnit and TPL/TexWk/GX texture declarations; real KOS pvr_vertex_t/poly-header/poly-context definitions with size/alignment/offset assertions.",
    "Texture Package/Header/Texture layout and used getters/pvr_format; real KOS pvr_poly_cxt_txr/pvr_poly_compile and native TEX_MIP_DADJ wrapper; actual begin_pvr_packet.",
    "re4dc_draw_id_quad and its inline projection; re4dc_ui_submit; ui_draw_quad/ui_order_flush; original non-SS_UI_ORDER quad loop extracted from present; glyph_header/glyph_draw_run; overlay_depth.",
    "messageCamera, C_MTXOrtho/C_MTXIdentity/C_MTXConcat, CameraSetProjection/CameraCurrentProjection, GXProject and GX projection/viewport functions; gx_fast.h inline getter/setter arithmetic."
  ],
  "fixture_adaptations": [
    "Host pointer width and synthetic 32-bit opaque texture/palette addresses; explicit 104-byte target-field serialization for bridge observations.",
    "Texture Package private access made public only in generated fixture so synthetic backing/header/VRAM pointer fields can be populated; destructor is a no-op fixture edge. No source data file/loading/residency behavior is claimed.",
    "KOS MOVCA replaced with scalar first-word store and explicit unspecified-tail marker; only first 4 compiled header words have a hardware-defined claim.",
    "Retail 8 MiB VRAM pointer mask and pointer-width-safe KOS cast; actual header/compiler/type bodies retained.",
    "Native texture resolve/load, stream transport, IdGetTexWk/TEXGet and presentation callbacks are controlled recorded edges. Arguments/order are compared; separate ownership/residency implementations are unchanged and not revalidated.",
    "Projection and queue observation hooks are fixture-only. GX no-op call counters are coverage, not equality outputs. The empty SH4 FP barrier in gx_fast.h uses an x86 SSE register constraint on the host.",
    "Bridge matrix concatenation uses actual C_MTXConcat as the unchanged math edge; this does not independently establish the selected target assembly matrix kernel.",
    "Frame setup follows synthetic boundary cases; full native frame/presenter/movie owner is not included. Both original quad draining bodies and original glyph flush logic are included."
  ],
